WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:04.240
Okay.

00:04.280 --> 00:05.840
So now what is the definition of the.

00:05.880 --> 00:09.080
And it says all conditions must be true.

00:09.080 --> 00:14.080
So all the conditions that you have in the Where clause must be true in order to keep the row in the

00:14.080 --> 00:14.680
results.

00:14.720 --> 00:16.400
So let's understand what this means.

00:16.440 --> 00:21.840
Things can get more complicated where you can have not only one condition, but you might have multiple

00:21.840 --> 00:23.280
conditions in your query.

00:23.280 --> 00:28.680
So here we can add a second condition where we're going to say not only the country must be equal to

00:28.720 --> 00:32.600
USA, but also the score must be higher than 500.

00:32.640 --> 00:36.520
So now you have two conditions and you have to put them in the Where clause.

00:36.560 --> 00:40.440
Now you have to combine those conditions using the logical operator.

00:40.440 --> 00:45.320
And here we have two options two operators the and operator and the or operator.

00:45.320 --> 00:51.840
In this scenario if you say and then SQL is very restrictive, both of the conditions must be true in

00:51.840 --> 00:54.120
order to keep the row in the results.

00:54.120 --> 00:55.560
So now let's see how this can work.

00:55.560 --> 01:01.560
Now for the first row and for the first condition you can see the country is Germany and it is not fulfilling

01:01.600 --> 01:02.880
the first condition.

01:02.880 --> 01:04.200
So this is going to be false.

01:04.200 --> 01:08.920
And as well if you check the second condition for the first row, you can see the score is 350.

01:08.960 --> 01:13.330
So that means this customer is as well, not fulfilling even the second condition.

01:13.330 --> 01:16.210
So both of the conditions is false and it's going to go.

01:16.250 --> 01:18.090
I remove this customer from the results.

01:18.130 --> 01:19.130
Now to the next one.

01:19.130 --> 01:19.610
John.

01:19.610 --> 01:25.610
You can see John is fulfilling the first condition because the country is equal to USA and as well fulfilling

01:25.610 --> 01:29.690
the second condition, his score is 900 and this is higher than 500.

01:29.690 --> 01:33.410
So now it's going to be very happy about it because both of them is true.

01:33.410 --> 01:38.610
And this is the only way in order to keep the row in the output because we are using the operator.

01:38.610 --> 01:41.010
And so John can stay in the outputs.

01:41.050 --> 01:42.290
Now moving on to George.

01:42.290 --> 01:46.490
He is not fulfilling the first condition, but now the second condition is fulfilled.

01:46.530 --> 01:49.690
His score is 750 and this is higher than 500.

01:49.730 --> 01:52.250
So now it's like 5050 right in one side.

01:52.250 --> 01:54.170
It's false but the other side is true.

01:54.170 --> 01:56.730
But this is not enough for the and operator.

01:56.770 --> 01:59.770
Both of them should be true in order to keep the result in the output.

01:59.770 --> 02:01.890
That's why SQL is going to remove this row.

02:01.930 --> 02:02.930
Now moving on to Martin.

02:02.930 --> 02:04.930
He is not fulfilling both of the conditions.

02:04.930 --> 02:07.730
So it's going to go and remove it from the results.

02:07.730 --> 02:11.210
And now for the last one Peter is fulfilling the first condition.

02:11.210 --> 02:15.650
The country is equal to USA but the second condition is sadly not fulfilled.

02:15.650 --> 02:18.290
So we have the score zero not higher than 500.

02:18.330 --> 02:19.890
Again we have the same scenario.

02:19.890 --> 02:23.260
It's 5050 and this is not enough for the end operator.

02:23.300 --> 02:25.180
That's why SQL going to go and remove it.

02:25.180 --> 02:30.700
So as you can see, if you use an ant operator, a lot of rows are going to be removed if one of the

02:30.700 --> 02:32.140
condition is not met.

02:32.140 --> 02:34.340
So the ant operator is very restrictive.

02:34.380 --> 02:38.220
Both of the conditions must be fulfilled to keep the row in the results.

02:38.220 --> 02:41.340
So this is exactly how the and operator works.

02:41.380 --> 02:41.580
Okay.

02:41.620 --> 02:42.780
So now we have the following task.

02:42.780 --> 02:48.420
Retrieve all customers who are from USA and have a score greater than 500.

02:48.460 --> 02:50.900
So here we are like combining multiple conditions.

02:50.900 --> 02:52.500
And let's go and do it step by step.

02:52.500 --> 02:55.980
So the first thing that we have to go and select the data from the correct table.

02:55.980 --> 02:58.420
So select star from customers.

02:58.420 --> 03:00.820
And with that we are getting all the customers from the table.

03:00.860 --> 03:04.700
Now the first condition we need the customers that come from USA.

03:04.740 --> 03:06.940
So we need only those two customers.

03:06.940 --> 03:11.340
And in order to do that as we learned, we can go and use the Where clause and the condition is going

03:11.340 --> 03:14.300
to be country equal to USA.

03:14.460 --> 03:17.540
So if we go and execute, we will get those two customers.

03:17.580 --> 03:18.500
Nothing is new.

03:18.540 --> 03:22.380
We have used the comparison operator equal but we are not done yet.

03:22.380 --> 03:24.900
We have another condition from those two customers.

03:24.900 --> 03:29.340
We need only the customers where their score is higher than 500.

03:29.340 --> 03:31.270
So now by looking to those two customers.

03:31.270 --> 03:35.950
You can see we see that the bitter here does not have a score higher than 500.

03:35.990 --> 03:37.990
And we don't want to see that in the results.

03:37.990 --> 03:38.790
So now what you have to do.

03:38.790 --> 03:42.190
We have to go and write a condition for this one over here.

03:42.190 --> 03:45.350
So this is based this time on the scores not on the country.

03:45.350 --> 03:48.910
So the score should be greater than 500.

03:48.950 --> 03:54.390
Now as you can see we have the first condition for the first one here and the second condition for the

03:54.430 --> 03:55.870
second requirement.

03:55.910 --> 03:58.750
Now the question how to connect those two conditions.

03:58.750 --> 04:01.230
So here we have two options and or.

04:01.310 --> 04:03.030
And to be honest this is very simple.

04:03.030 --> 04:08.670
The task says it customer should fulfill both of the conditions should be from USA and as well at the

04:08.670 --> 04:11.110
same time greater than 500.

04:11.110 --> 04:12.990
So it is very simple we're going to say.

04:13.030 --> 04:16.030
And so with that we have connected both of those conditions.

04:16.030 --> 04:21.590
And if you go and query it you will get only one customer that is fulfilling our conditions.

04:21.590 --> 04:27.630
So from all customers we have only one customer that fulfilled this condition that comes from USA.

04:27.630 --> 04:32.150
And at the same time the score of this customer is higher than 500.

04:32.150 --> 04:36.830
So this is how we use the and operator in order to connect to conditions.
